From 251d824ec71168ec7103d96209178babaf9d8360 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hdmi-los-builder <hdmi-los@localhost>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:28:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] composer: lease an overlay plane for the Xorg cursor

Optional experiment paired with the optional Xserver OverlayCursor patch.
Leasing a distinct plane rendered the pointer correctly, but did not fix the
measured pointer-motion cadence and is therefore not in the default series.

Qualcomm SDE exposes primary and overlay planes but no DRM cursor plane and no
legacy CRTC cursor callbacks.  Consequently, upstream modesetting falls back
to a software cursor whose save/restore damage serializes the full KGSL-to-KMS
presentation bridge on every pointer update.

Select one ARGB8888-capable overlay compatible with the external CRTC while
the final handoff is serialized.  Prefer an overlay already used by that
external CRTC, otherwise use an unassigned overlay; never take a plane assigned
to another CRTC.  Sanitize the selected object with the other external planes,
verify that it is detached, and add it to the DRM lease.  This lets the private
Xorg modesetting driver use the standard KMS plane API for the cursor without
touching the primary framebuffer.

Track the extra plane through revocation so a forced client exit cannot return
stale cursor state to Android.  If the hardware has no compatible overlay,
preserve the existing three-object lease and Xorg's software-cursor fallback.
Enumeration or validation failures still fail closed.
